WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.651
Every fire, from a candle to a spacecraft emergency, needs three things at once: fuel, oxygen, and heat.

2
00:00:08.057 --> 00:00:11.227
Take any one of them away, and the fire goes out.

3
00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:18.332
That simple triangle is the basis of fire safety: prevent, detect, and suppress.

4
00:00:18.808 --> 00:00:21.803
Most fires in a cabin are diffusion flames.

5
00:00:22.128 --> 00:00:28.642
Fuel and oxygen start apart, and they only burn where they meet, in a thin glowing layer.

6
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:37.407
Every fuel uses a fixed amount of oxygen. One molecule of propane needs five molecules of oxygen to burn completely.

7
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.621
If the oxygen near the flame runs low, the burning slows down.

8
00:00:42.236 --> 00:00:48.123
NASA has tested three kinds of fuel in microgravity: gases, liquid droplets, and solids.

9
00:00:48.576 --> 00:00:57.294
This database holds 660 gas flame tests, 353 droplet tests, and 263 tests of solid materials.

10
00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:05.340
Solids matter most, because a spacecraft is full of them: fabric, plastic, and wiring.
